{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04SX", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-definition-representable-map-categories-fibred-in-groupoids}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:72cbe2cecf58a09c61bbdc294f945544a0bbbb647abc264fff34542995c113e7", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn analogy with Categories, Definition\n<REF_0001>\nwe make the following definition.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0109c57be24d4bd438b62f7e114c10b7f98e008a33e926ed6ca48336b4f25bbc", "unit_id": "tag:04SX:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "04SX", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$1$", "MATH_0004": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0005": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\in \\Ob((\\Sch/S)_{fppf})$", "MATH_0007": "$y : (\\Sch/U)_{fppf} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n(\\Sch/U)_{fppf} \\times_{y, \\mathcal{Y}} \\mathcal{X}\n$$", "MATH_0009": "$(\\Sch/U)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0010": "$U$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-representable-by-algebraic-spaces}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d61839cd61a67f4b28e731b624a413b8edaccbaeb381f0b284fc3b4511c0e891", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:64ef6d3b24efc3000f8f67ae9fd5e4996292cfc9cf89e418b4d3b5643fc247bb", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme contained in <MATH_0002>.\nA <MATH_0003>-morphism <MATH_0004> of\ncategories fibred in groupoids over <MATH_0005>\nis called <TEXTITOPEN_0001>representable by algebraic spaces<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if\nfor any <MATH_0006>\nand any <MATH_0007>\nthe category fibred in groupoids\n<MATH_0008>\nover <MATH_0009>\nis representable by an algebraic space over <MATH_0010>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bec6a8a689daff14faf1808e90a9cd17e30d9329f654a8f11dc1f1db7fbc6b59", "unit_id": "tag:02ZW:statement"}
{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04SX", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F_y$", "MATH_0002": "$U$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\Sch/U)_{fppf} \\times_{y, \\mathcal{Y}} \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$F_y$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "MATH_0006": "$f_y : F_y \\to U$", "MATH_0007": "$S$", "MATH_0008": "\\begin{equation}\n\\label{equation-representable-by-algebraic-spaces}\n\\vcenter{\n\\xymatrix{\nF_y \\ar[d]_{f_y} &\n(\\Sch/U)_{fppf} \\times_{y, \\mathcal{Y}} \\mathcal{X}\n\\ar@{~>}[l] \\ar[d]_{\\text{pr}_0} \\ar[r]_-{\\text{pr}_1} &\n\\mathcal{X} \\ar[d]^f \\\\\nU &\n(\\Sch/U)_{fppf} \\ar@{~>}[l] \\ar[r]^-y &\n\\mathcal{Y}\n}\n}\n\\end{equation}", "MATH_0009": "$2$", "MATH_0010": "$2$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-section-change-base-scheme}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{categories-lemma-criterion-representable-map-stack-in-groupoids}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:bd25e68ccb7ad2aeae64be722d7cbcc1823340c67920ef24a3bc815002550e62", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8751ae28973bfe72ca5dbdc037fb31115e68d8f5260580ec8d3a0a9a4b836166", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nChoose an algebraic space <MATH_0001> over <MATH_0002> which represents\n<MATH_0003>.\nWe may think of <MATH_0004> as an algebraic space over <MATH_0005>\nwhich comes equipped with a canonical morphism <MATH_0006>\nover <MATH_0007>, see\nSpaces, Section <REF_0001>.\nHere is the diagram\n<MATH_0008>\nwhere the squiggly arrows represent the construction which associates\nto a stack fibred in setoids its associated sheaf of isomorphism classes\nof objects. The right square is\n<MATH_0009>-commutative, and is a <MATH_0010>-fibre product square.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nHere is the analogue of Categories,\nLemma <REF_0002>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f44408fead9519ad492e5698c809362192692d3e641b579223da39744b4fd0f4", "unit_id": "tag:04SX:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04SX", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0004": "$1$", "MATH_0005": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$U/S$", "MATH_0008": "$f_U : \\mathcal{X}_U \\longrightarrow \\mathcal{Y}_U$", "MATH_0009": "$U$", "MATH_0010": "$y \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{Y}_U)$", "MATH_0011": "$$\n(h : V \\to U)\n\\longmapsto\n\\{(x, \\phi) \\mid x \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{X}_V), \\phi : h^*y \\to f(x)\\}/\\cong\n$$", "MATH_0012": "$U$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-criterion-map-representable-spaces-fibred-in-groupoids}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c037c8b586025a40a07ea00c8c28627f68c643fa950e4a3b8b586c91659cf5bf", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:97064543e564fe63005525aec88ef6ed9c345439c3b1aa4f86af6c4326fe268c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme contained in <MATH_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a <MATH_0004>-morphism\nof categories fibred in groupoids over <MATH_0005>.\nThe following are necessary and sufficient conditions for\n<MATH_0006> to be representable by algebraic spaces:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> for each scheme <MATH_0007> the\nfunctor <MATH_0008>\nbetween fibre categories is faithful, and\n<STRUCT_0003> for each <MATH_0009> and each <MATH_0010> the presheaf\n<MATH_0011>\nis an algebraic space over <MATH_0012>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nHere we have made a choice of pullbacks for <MATH_0013>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:26663c79a187441cc4b0694aaa7691da35c874c617b3e567d98d711066fc5511", "unit_id": "tag:02ZY:statement"}
